    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are primed for a high-ceiling offensive output today, headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 74.56 score makes him our premier start. He faces a favorable matchup against Pecko (5.95 xERA), benefiting significantly from a +19% SP skill boost and a +14% platoon edge. Similarly, **Kyle Tucker** (71.13) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (72.39) anchor the core, with **Tucker** enjoying a soft matchup against Elder and **Guerrero Jr.** poised to capitalize on his +13% SP skill projection against a vulnerable Lugo. These three represent our highest probability of driving runs and home runs, providing the stability required for a competitive 5x5 Roto push.\n\nNavigating the scarcity of stolen bases remains a priority, though the day carries significant friction. **Luis Robert Jr.** (49.76) and **Jackson Merrill** (48.86) both face elite-level holds and tough arms, forcing a marginal dip in their efficiency scores. We have opted to bench **Miguel Vargas** (39.33), who fell just shy of our 40-point floor; while his underlying xwOBA remains encouraging, the daunting matchup against deGrom\u2014compounded by the aggressive defensive setups\u2014renders him a risky play compared to the higher-upside profiles in our active lineup.\n\nCaution is warranted for the bottom half of the order, particularly regarding **Nasim Nunez** (42.76) and **Sam Antonacci** (43.60), who are tasked with navigating high-leverage arms like Adams and deGrom, respectively. While **Gunnar Henderson** (53.96) and **Coby Mayo** (54.09) are facing a tougher-than-average start from Liberatore, their roster positions are secure due to their overall reliability. Managers should closely monitor the defensive adjustments for **Merrill** and **Robert Jr.**, as their speed upside is neutralized today by high-efficiency catching backstops and elite pick-off sequences. With **Andy Pages**, **Jordan Westburg**, and **Heliot Ramos** currently unavailable, our margin for error is 